      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "631be9ba1672ef44b9392793",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I want to do a quick bump of this post. As part of the developer update today https://ask.vrchat.com/t/developer-update-16-february-2023/16474 we are going to eventually be limited by how many constraints we can use in our project.\n\nCurrently there is a method to create fake local constraints by making THREE duplicates of your entire avatar and animating constraints across all copies. For my current model, this is approximately 300 constraints just to make a local constrained version of my avatar. I am absolutely animating these off whenever not in use, but it sounds like regardless, they will affect the ranking of my avatar.\n\nIf we were given the ability to do local constraints with an official tool, this would be significantly reduced.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "63ef4c81ab4363450df6f0a3",
      "author": {
        "_id": "62229f03e709ef2a451af502",
        "alias": "Evergreen Firefly",
        "aliasID": "65c2b901ed6eefce4c736ffe",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/03f383b8165ac07479283fdd0c262471.png",
        "created": "2022-03-04T23:21:39.743Z",
        "name": "Ahzealion",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5ed571497ee72a2434704a15",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2023-02-17T09:44:33.938Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": "669054b67e5d7ce9c644bc40",
      "mergedPostDetails": "My original post on this topic is quite old and also marked as \"feedback\" when it is actually a feature request.\n\nThe developer update today covers some information about the limitations of constraints. https://ask.vrchat.com/t/developer-update-16-february-2023/16474 It seems that eventually our avatars will be ranked based on the number of constraints.\n\nI would like to recommend that we include the ability to do local constraints using an official VRChat script.\n\nCurrently the only other way to make local constraints involves having three extra armatures all with constraints attached to them. For a typical avatar, this will account for 200 to 300 extra constraints that could be replaced by a small number of local constraints.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Local Constraints",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "631be9ba1672ef44b9392793",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 3
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I would also reckon that a lot of the avatars with high amounts of constraints (that are causing problem) are often trying to emulate local constraints in some way shape or form, Like the avatar clone tools, and are not performant for that exact reason. Since it takes some extreme Jank to emulate what local constraints would do.\n\nLocal constraints would just be a great addition overall and would alleviate a lot of the current \"my avatar has 600 constraints on it\" situations.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
